  RUMOAR sitemap.

  A NOTE ON THE HASH URLS, because it matters and pretending otherwise would
  be worse than the problem: this store uses a hash router (#/shop) so that a
  deep link works on any static host with no rewrite rules — GitHub Pages, a
  CDN, even dist/index.html opened off a disk. The cost is that search engines
  treat everything after the # as the same page, so these entries are a hint
  about site structure rather than six separately-indexable URLs.

  If organic search becomes a primary channel, switch to history routing —
  the exact change is documented in README.md under "The one SEO trade-off".
  It is about twenty lines and one rewrite rule.
-->
